se trends in the diagnosis and management of prostate cancer in USA</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>1995</year><volume>154</volume><fpage>207</fpage><lpage>208</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Urol||154|207||bib11|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7539862</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Gleave</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Goldenberg</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Chin</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Warner</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Saad</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Klotz</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Jewett</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Kassalian</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Chetner</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Dupont</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Van Reusselaer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><collab>the Canadian Uro-Oncology Group</collab></person-group><article-title>Randomized comparative study of 3 versus 8-month neoadjuvant hormonal therapy before radical prostatectomy: biochemical and pathological effects</article-title><source>J Urol</source><year>2001</year><volume>166</volume><fpage>500</fpage><lpage>507</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Urol||166|500||bib12|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11458055</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib13"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Palanham</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Headley</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardiner</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Altered cognitive functioning in men treated for prostate cancer with luteinizing hormone-releasing hormone analogues and cyprotenone acetate: a randomized controlled trial</article-title><source>BJU Int</source><year>2002a</year><volume>90</volume><fpage>427</fpage><lpage>432</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'BJU Int||90|427||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12175403</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Green</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><name><surname>Palanham</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Headley</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Gardiner</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Coping and health-related quality of life in men with prostate cancer randomly assigned to hormonal medicationor close monitoring</article-title><source>Psycho-oncology</source><year>2002b</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>401</fpage><lpage>414</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Psycho-oncology||11|401||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12228873</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kujala</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Portin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Revonsuo</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruukainen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Automatic and controlled information processing in multiple sclerosis</article-title><source>Brain</source><year>1994</year><volume>117</volume><fpage>1115</fpage><lpage>1126</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Brain||117|1115||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7953593</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kujala</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Portin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ruutiainen</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The progress of cognitive decline in multiple sclerosis &#x02013; a controlled 3-year follow-up</article-title><source>Brain</source><year>1997</year><volume>120</volume><fpage>289</fpage><lpage>297</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Brain||120|289||bib16|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9117376</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib17"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lezak</surname><given-names>MD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title/><source>Neuropsychological assessment</source><year>1995</year><publisher-name>New York: Oxford University Press</publisher-name>3rd edn</citation></ref><ref id="bib18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Lilja</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Portin</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Hamalainen</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Salminen</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Short-term effects of radiotherapy on attention and memory performances in patients with brain tumours</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>2001</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>2361</fpage><lpage>2368</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer||91|2361||bib18|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11413526</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib19"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Littell</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Milliken</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Stroup</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Wolfinger</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name></person-group><article-title/><source>SAS&#x000ae; System for Mixed Models</source><year>1996</year><publisher-name>Cary, NC: